# ── Brand assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the files the site actually uses are tracked. Git keeps every version
# of a binary forever, and two of the originals are documented as unusable in
# production: stella_ltr_logo.png has a broken alpha channel, and
# icon_images/chead-*.jpg carry five-star rating badges baked into the pixels
# (§13, §71). The full 23 MB original set stays on disk, untracked, at
# images/ — see docs/architecture/REPOSITORY_AUDIT.md.
images/*
!images/stella_hero_bg1.png
!images/logo
images/logo/*
!images/logo/stella.png

# Generated web assets. Derived from images/ by scripts/build-assets.mjs — do
# not commit them: git keeps binary history forever, and every re-export would
# add another permanent copy. Run `npm run build:assets` to regenerate.
apps/customer-web/public/*.webp
apps/customer-web/public/favicon.png

# Source artwork required to reproduce the landing hero.
!images/herosection/
images/herosection/*
!images/herosection/hero_bg.png
!images/celestial/
images/celestial/*
!images/celestial/assembly.png
!images/celestial/PROMPT.md

!images/celestial/separated-sheet.png

# OAuth client secret files downloaded from Google Cloud Console. One landed in
# docs/ on 2026-09-15 and was caught before it was committed; this makes the
# next one impossible rather than lucky. Real values live in
# /home/stellaastro/secrets/.
client_secret_*.json
*-oauth-client.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
